{
  "_what_this_is": [
    "Pixel reftests: a page, and assertions about what it must look like.",
    "Run by `make render-conformance` (tools/conformance/render_check.py),",
    "which reads the PNG with its own decoder so the engine is not asked to",
    "grade its own writer.",
    "",
    "An assertion is one of:",
    "  pixel      a point is a colour (tolerance optional, 0 by default)",
    "  rect       a rectangle is uniformly a colour",
    "  uniform    a rectangle is one colour, whichever it is",
    "  not-colour a point is anything but a colour",
    "  differs    two points are not the same colour (something was painted)",
    "",
    "Coordinates are CSS pixels from the top left of the 800x600 viewport.",
    "Exact equality is the default on purpose: box edges here are not",
    "anti-aliased, so an off-by-one is a bug rather than a rounding.",
    "",
    "A test may carry `known_failure`: a sentence saying what the spec requires",
    "and the engine does not do yet. The run prints KNOWN with the reason, and",
    "counts it as neither a pass nor a failure. The entry is a debt, not a",
    "silence: if the page starts passing, the run prints FIXED and exits 1, so",
    "the reason has to come out in the same commit that fixes the bug.",
    "Five pages carry one since Phase 133 (finding 138): paint order for floats and for transformed elements, a clip that is square where the radius is round, and two found while fixing cross-axis alignment \u2014 `justify-content` in a column container and `align-self`. The three alignment pages recorded by Phase 122 (finding 127) lost their reasons here, which is the ledger working in the direction that matters.",
    "and transformed elements, cross-axis alignment in flex and grid, and a clip",
    "that is square where the radius is round."
  ],
  "tests": [
    {
      "name": "a_block_paints_its_background_exactly",
      "html": "<!doctype html><html><head><style>\n  body { margin: 0 }\n  .box { width: 50px; height: 50px; background: #ff0000 }\n</style></head><body><div class=\"box\"></div></body></html>",
      "assert": [
        {
          "kind": "rect",
          "x": 0,
          "y": 0,
          "width": 50,
          "height": 50,
          "colour": "#ff0000",
          "describe": "the 50x50 block is red throughout"
        },
        {
          "kind": "pixel",
          "x": 0,
          "y": 0,
          "colour": "#ff0000",
          "describe": "its top-left corner is inside it"
        },
        {
          "kind": "pixel",
          "x": 49,
          "y": 49,
          "colour": "#ff0000",
          "describe": "its bottom-right corner is inside it"
        },
        {
          "kind": "pixel",
          "x": 50,
          "y": 0,
          "colour": "#ffffff",
          "describe": "one pixel to its right is not (no overflow)"
        },
        {
          "kind": "pixel",
          "x": 0,
          "y": 50,
          "colour": "#ffffff",
          "describe": "one pixel below it is not"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "stacked_blocks_stack_in_document_order",
      "html": "<!doctype html><html><head><style>\n  body { margin: 0 }\n  .a { width: 40px; height: 30px; background: #0000ff }\n  .b { width: 40px; height: 30px; background: #00ff00 }\n</style></head><body><div class=\"a\"></div><div class=\"b\"></div></body></html>",
      "assert": [
        {
          "kind": "rect",
          "x": 0,
          "y": 0,
          "width": 40,
          "height": 30,
          "colour": "#0000ff",
          "describe": "the first block is blue"
        },
        {
          "kind": "rect",
          "x": 0,
          "y": 30,
          "width": 40,
          "height": 30,
          "colour": "#00ff00",
          "describe": "the second starts where the first ended"
        },
        {
          "kind": "pixel",
          "x": 0,
          "y": 60,
          "colour": "#ffffff",
          "describe": "and nothing is painted below the second"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "margin_left_moves_the_box_and_leaves_its_margin_blank",
      "html": "<!doctype html><html><head><style>\n  body { margin: 0 }\n  .box { margin-left: 80px; width: 25px; height: 20px; background: #00ff00 }\n</style></head><body><div class=\"box\"></div></body></html>",
      "assert": [
        {
          "kind": "rect",
          "x": 80,
          "y": 0,
          "width": 25,
          "height": 20,
          "colour": "#00ff00",
          "describe": "the box begins at its margin-left"
        },
        {
          "kind": "pixel",
          "x": 79,
          "y": 5,
          "colour": "#ffffff",
          "describe": "the margin to its left is unpainted"
        },
        {
          "kind": "pixel",
          "x": 105,
          "y": 5,
          "colour": "#ffffff",
          "describe": "and nothing overflows to its right"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "borders_paint_around_the_content_and_the_content_stays_inside",
      "html": "<!doctype html><html><head><style>\n  body { margin: 0 }\n  .box { border: 4px solid #008000; width: 30px; height: 20px; background: #0000ff }\n</style></head><body><div class=\"box\"></div></body></html>",
      "assert": [
        {
          "kind": "rect",
          "x": 0,
          "y": 0,
          "width": 38,
          "height": 4,
          "colour": "#008000",
          "describe": "the top border is 4px of the border colour, across the padding box"
        },
        {
          "kind": "rect",
          "x": 0,
          "y": 0,
          "width": 4,
          "height": 28,
          "colour": "#008000",
          "describe": "the left border is 4px down the full border box"
        },
        {
          "kind": "rect",
          "x": 4,
          "y": 4,
          "width": 30,
          "height": 20,
          "colour": "#0000ff",
          "describe": "the content is inside the border, not under it"
        },
        {
          "kind": "pixel",
          "x": 38,
          "y": 10,
          "colour": "#ffffff",
          "describe": "nothing is painted past the border box"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "padding_moves_the_content_without_painting",
      "html": "<!doctype html><html><head><style>\n  body { margin: 0 }\n  .outer { padding: 20px; width: 40px; height: 40px; background: #ff00ff }\n  .inner { width: 10px; height: 10px; background: #000000 }\n</style></head><body><div class=\"outer\"><div class=\"inner\"></div></div></body></html>",
      "assert": [
        {
          "kind": "rect",
          "x": 0,
          "y": 0,
          "width": 60,
          "height": 20,
          "colour": "#ff00ff",
          "describe": "the padding band above the content is the outer background"
        },
        {
          "kind": "rect",
          "x": 20,
          "y": 20,
          "width": 10,
          "height": 10,
          "colour": "#000000",
          "describe": "the content box begins after 20px of padding"
        },
        {
          "kind": "pixel",
          "x": 19,
          "y": 25,
          "colour": "#ff00ff",
          "describe": "and the padding to its left is still the outer background"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "text_is_painted_where_its_line_box_starts",
      "html": "<!doctype html><html><head><style>\n  body { margin: 0; font-size: 32px }\n</style></head><body>x</body></html>",
      "assert": [
        {
          "kind": "differs",
          "ax": 8,
          "ay": 20,
          "bx": 200,
          "by": 300,
          "a-besides": "#ffffff",
          "describe": "the glyph's stem is painted in the line box and is not the page colour, while the page below is blank"
        },
        {
          "kind": "rect",
          "x": 0,
          "y": 60,
          "width": 200,
          "height": 60,
          "colour": "#ffffff",
          "describe": "nothing is painted below the single line of text"
        }
      ],
      "note": "The glyph's exact grey is font-dependent, so this asserts where the ink is and that the page below it is untouched, rather than a colour."
    },
    {
      "name": "a_later_block_covers_an_earlier_one",
      "html": "<!doctype html><html><head><style>\n  body { margin: 0; position: relative }\n  .under { width: 60px; height: 60px; background: #ff0000 }\n  .over  { position: absolute; left: 10px; top: 10px; width: 20px; height: 20px; background: #0000ff }\n</style></head><body><div class=\"under\"></div><div class=\"over\"></div></body></html>",
      "assert": [
        {
          "kind": "rect",
          "x": 10,
          "y": 10,
          "width": 20,
          "height": 20,
          "colour": "#0000ff",
          "describe": "the absolutely positioned box paints over the one before it"
        },
        {
          "kind": "pixel",
          "x": 5,
          "y": 5,
          "colour": "#ff0000",
          "describe": "and the box underneath still shows where it is not covered"
        },
        {
          "kind": "pixel",
          "x": 30,
          "y": 30,
          "colour": "#ff0000",
          "describe": "including one pixel past the covering box"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "display_none_paints_nothing",
      "html": "<!doctype html><html><head><style>\n  body { margin: 0 }\n  .shown { width: 30px; height: 30px; background: #0000ff }\n  .hidden { display: none; width: 100px; height: 100px; background: #ff0000 }\n</style></head><body><div class=\"shown\"></div><div class=\"hidden\"></div></body></html>",
      "assert": [
        {
          "kind": "rect",
          "x": 0,
          "y": 0,
          "width": 30,
          "height": 30,
          "colour": "#0000ff",
          "describe": "the shown box is painted"
        },
        {
          "kind": "rect",
          "x": 0,
          "y": 30,
          "width": 200,
          "height": 100,
          "colour": "#ffffff",
          "describe": "and the display:none box occupies no pixels at all"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "a_percentage_width_is_resolved_against_the_viewport",
      "html": "<!doctype html><html><head><style>\n  body { margin: 0 }\n  .half { width: 50%; height: 20px; background: #008000 }\n</style></head><body><div class=\"half\"></div></body></html>",
      "assert": [
        {
          "kind": "pixel",
          "x": 0,
          "y": 10,
          "colour": "#008000",
          "describe": "the half-width box starts at the left edge"
        },
        {
          "kind": "pixel",
          "x": 399,
          "y": 10,
          "colour": "#008000",
          "describe": "50% of an 800px viewport still covers x=399"
        },
        {
          "kind": "pixel",
          "x": 400,
          "y": 10,
          "colour": "#ffffff",
          "describe": "and stops at x=400"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "an_offscreen_box_paints_inside_the_image_only",
      "html": "<!doctype html><html><head><style>\n  body { margin: 0 }\n  .a { width: 700px; height: 10px; background: #ff0000 }\n  .b { width: 400px; height: 10px; background: #0000ff }\n</style></head><body><div class=\"a\"></div><div class=\"b\"></div></body></html>",
      "assert": [
        {
          "kind": "pixel",
          "x": 699,
          "y": 5,
          "colour": "#ff0000",
          "describe": "the wide box reaches the last pixel it should"
        },
        {
          "kind": "pixel",
          "x": 799,
          "y": 5,
          "colour": "#ffffff",
          "describe": "and no further"
        },
        {
          "kind": "pixel",
          "x": 399,
          "y": 15,
          "colour": "#0000ff",
          "describe": "the second box is clipped at the viewport edge, not scrolled into view"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "flex_space_between_puts_the_outer_items_at_the_edges",
      "html": "<!doctype html><html><head><style>\n  body { margin: 0 }\n.c { display: flex; width: 200px; height: 60px; justify-content: space-between }.i { width: 40px; height: 60px }\n</style></head><body><div class=\"c\"><div class=\"i\" style=\"background:#ff0000\"></div><div class=\"i\" style=\"background:#00ff00\"></div><div class=\"i\" style=\"background:#0000ff\"></div></div></body></html>",
      "assert": [
        {
          "kind": "rect",
          "x": 0,
          "y": 0,
          "width": 40,
          "height": 60,
          "colour": "#ff0000",
          "describe": "the first item is flush with the left edge"
        },
        {
          "kind": "pixel",
          "x": 79,
          "y": 30,
          "colour": "#ffffff",
          "describe": "the first gap is empty"
        },
        {
          "kind": "pixel",
          "x": 80,
          "y": 30,
          "colour": "#00ff00",
          "describe": "the second starts at 80"
        },
        {
          "kind": "pixel",
          "x": 119,
          "y": 30,
          "colour": "#00ff00",
          "describe": "and ends at 119"
        },
        {
          "kind": "pixel",
          "x": 120,
          "y": 30,
          "colour": "#ffffff",
          "describe": "the second gap is empty"
        },
        {
          "kind": "pixel",
          "x": 160,
          "y": 30,
          "colour": "#0000ff",
          "describe": "the third starts at 160"
        },
        {
          "kind": "rect",
          "x": 160,
          "y": 0,
          "width": 40,
          "height": 60,
          "colour": "#0000ff",
          "describe": "and is flush with the right edge"
        },
        {
          "kind": "pixel",
          "x": 200,
          "y": 30,
          "colour": "#ffffff",
          "describe": "nothing is painted past 200"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "flex_column_stacks_items_downward",
      "html": "<!doctype html><html><head><style>\n  body { margin: 0 }\n.c { display: flex; flex-direction: column; width: 100px; height: 100px }.a { height: 30px; background: #ff0000 } .b { height: 20px; background: #0000ff }\n</style></head><body><div class=\"c\"><div class=\"a\"></div><div class=\"b\"></div></div></body></html>",
      "assert": [
        {
          "kind": "rect",
          "x": 0,
          "y": 0,
          "width": 100,
          "height": 30,
          "colour": "#ff0000",
          "describe": "the first item is 30 tall"
        },
        {
          "kind": "pixel",
          "x": 0,
          "y": 30,
          "colour": "#0000ff",
          "describe": "the second begins at y=30"
        },
        {
          "kind": "rect",
          "x": 0,
          "y": 30,
          "width": 100,
          "height": 20,
          "colour": "#0000ff",
          "describe": "and is 20 tall"
        },
        {
          "kind": "pixel",
          "x": 0,
          "y": 50,
          "colour": "#ffffff",
          "describe": "nothing is painted below it"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "flex_wrap_puts_an_overflowing_item_on_the_next_line",
      "html": "<!doctype html><html><head><style>\n  body { margin: 0 }\n.c { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; width: 100px; height: 100px }.i { width: 60px; height: 20px }\n</style></head><body><div class=\"c\"><div class=\"i\" style=\"background:#ff0000\"></div><div class=\"i\" style=\"background:#00ff00\"></div><div class=\"i\" style=\"background:#0000ff\"></div></div></body></html>",
      "assert": [
        {
          "kind": "rect",
          "x": 0,
          "y": 0,
          "width": 60,
          "height": 20,
          "colour": "#ff0000",
          "describe": "the first line holds one item"
        },
        {
          "kind": "pixel",
          "x": 10,
          "y": 30,
          "colour": "#00ff00",
          "describe": "the second wrapped to y=20"
        },
        {
          "kind": "pixel",
          "x": 10,
          "y": 50,
          "colour": "#0000ff",
          "describe": "the third wrapped to y=40"
        },
        {
          "kind": "pixel",
          "x": 10,
          "y": 70,
          "colour": "#ffffff",
          "describe": "and the container is not filled"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "flex_justify_content_flex_end_packs_to_the_end",
      "html": "<!doctype html><html><head><style>\n  body { margin: 0 }\n.c { display: flex; justify-content: flex-end; width: 200px; height: 20px }.a { width: 50px; height: 20px; background: #ff0000 }\n</style></head><body><div class=\"c\"><div class=\"a\"></div></div></body></html>",
      "assert": [
        {
          "kind": "pixel",
          "x": 149,
          "y": 10,
          "colour": "#ffffff",
          "describe": "nothing is painted before the packed item"
        },
        {
          "kind": "rect",
          "x": 150,
          "y": 0,
          "width": 50,
          "height": 20,
          "colour": "#ff0000",
          "describe": "the item sits at 200-50 = 150"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "flex_justify_content_center_centres_the_line",
      "html": "<!doctype html><html><head><style>\n  body { margin: 0 }\n.c { display: flex; justify-content: center; width: 200px; height: 20px }.a { width: 60px; height: 20px; background: #0000ff }\n</style></head><body><div class=\"c\"><div class=\"a\"></div></div></body></html>",
      "assert": [
        {
          "kind": "pixel",
          "x": 69,
          "y": 10,
          "colour": "#ffffff",
          "describe": "nothing before the centred item"
        },
        {
          "kind": "rect",
          "x": 70,
          "y": 0,
          "width": 60,
          "height": 20,
          "colour": "#0000ff",
          "describe": "the line sits at (200-60)/2 = 70"
        },
        {
          "kind": "pixel",
          "x": 130,
          "y": 10,
          "colour": "#ffffff",
          "describe": "and nothing after it"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "flex_items_stretch_to_the_container_height",
      "html": "<!doctype html><html><head><style>\n  body { margin: 0 }\n.c { display: flex; width: 100px; height: 40px; background: #eeeeee }.a { width: 40px; background: #ff0000 }\n</style></head><body><div class=\"c\"><div class=\"a\"></div></div></body></html>",
      "assert": [
        {
          "kind": "rect",
          "x": 0,
          "y": 0,
          "width": 40,
          "height": 40,
          "colour": "#ff0000",
          "describe": "align-items: stretch (the default) makes the item 40 tall"
        },
        {
          "kind": "pixel",
          "x": 40,
          "y": 0,
          "colour": "#eeeeee",
          "describe": "and no wider than its 40px"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "flex_align_items_center_centres_a_shorter_item",
      "html": "<!doctype html><html><head><style>\n  body { margin: 0 }\n.c { display: flex; align-items: center; width: 100px; height: 100px; background: #eeeeee }.a { width: 50px; height: 20px; background: #ff0000 }\n</style></head><body><div class=\"c\"><div class=\"a\"></div></div></body></html>",
      "assert": [
        {
          "kind": "pixel",
          "x": 0,
          "y": 39,
          "colour": "#eeeeee",
          "describe": "above the item the container shows through"
        },
        {
          "kind": "rect",
          "x": 0,
          "y": 40,
          "width": 50,
          "height": 20,
          "colour": "#ff0000",
          "describe": "the item sits at (100-20)/2 = 40"
        },
        {
          "kind": "pixel",
          "x": 0,
          "y": 60,
          "colour": "#eeeeee",
          "describe": "and below it the container shows through"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "grid_items_stretch_to_their_area",
      "html": "<!doctype html><html><head><style>\n  body { margin: 0 }\n.g { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 60px 40px; grid-template-rows: 30px 20px }.a { background: #ff0000 } .b { background: #0000ff }\n</style></head><body><div class=\"g\"><div class=\"a\"></div><div class=\"b\"></div></div></body></html>",
      "assert": [
        {
          "kind": "rect",
          "x": 0,
          "y": 0,
          "width": 60,
          "height": 30,
          "colour": "#ff0000",
          "describe": "the first cell is 60x30 and its item fills it"
        },
        {
          "kind": "rect",
          "x": 60,
          "y": 0,
          "width": 40,
          "height": 30,
          "colour": "#0000ff",
          "describe": "the second cell is 40x30"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "grid_places_cells_on_its_tracks_and_honours_the_gap",
      "html": "<!doctype html><html><head><style>\n  body { margin: 0 }\n.g { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 60px 40px; grid-template-rows: 30px 20px; gap: 10px }.a { height: 30px; background: #ff0000 } .b { height: 30px; background: #00ff00 }\n  .c { height: 20px; background: #0000ff } .d { height: 20px; background: #ff00ff }\n</style></head><body><div class=\"g\"><div class=\"a\"></div><div class=\"b\"></div><div class=\"c\"></div><div class=\"d\"></div></div></body></html>",
      "assert": [
        {
          "kind": "rect",
          "x": 0,
          "y": 0,
          "width": 60,
          "height": 30,
          "colour": "#ff0000",
          "describe": "cell 1: first column, first row"
        },
        {
          "kind": "pixel",
          "x": 59,
          "y": 29,
          "colour": "#ff0000",
          "describe": "up to its last pixel"
        },
        {
          "kind": "pixel",
          "x": 60,
          "y": 0,
          "colour": "#ffffff",
          "describe": "the column gap is 10 wide and unpainted"
        },
        {
          "kind": "rect",
          "x": 70,
          "y": 0,
          "width": 40,
          "height": 30,
          "colour": "#00ff00",
          "describe": "cell 2 starts after the gap"
        },
        {
          "kind": "pixel",
          "x": 110,
          "y": 0,
          "colour": "#ffffff",
          "describe": "nothing is painted past the tracks"
        },
        {
          "kind": "pixel",
          "x": 0,
          "y": 39,
          "colour": "#ffffff",
          "describe": "the row gap is 10 tall"
        },
        {
          "kind": "rect",
          "x": 0,
          "y": 40,
          "width": 60,
          "height": 20,
          "colour": "#0000ff",
          "describe": "cell 3: first column, second row"
        },
        {
          "kind": "rect",
          "x": 70,
          "y": 40,
          "width": 40,
          "height": 20,
          "colour": "#ff00ff",
          "describe": "cell 4: second column, second row"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "a_float_is_painted_above_the_block_that_follows_it",
      "html": "<!doctype html><html><head><style>\n  body { margin: 0 }\n.f { float: left; width: 50px; height: 50px; background: #ff0000 }.b { width: 100px; height: 40px; background: #0000ff }.k { clear: both; width: 100px; height: 10px; background: #00ff00 }\n</style></head><body><div class=\"f\"></div><div class=\"b\"></div><div class=\"k\"></div></body></html>",
      "assert": [
        {
          "kind": "pixel",
          "x": 10,
          "y": 10,
          "colour": "#ff0000",
          "describe": "CSS 2.1 Appendix E paints floats above in-flow block backgrounds"
        },
        {
          "kind": "pixel",
          "x": 60,
          "y": 10,
          "colour": "#0000ff",
          "describe": "the block's background shows where the float is not"
        },
        {
          "kind": "pixel",
          "x": 10,
          "y": 45,
          "colour": "#ff0000",
          "describe": "the float is 50 tall and the block 40, so its last 10 rows are the float's"
        },
        {
          "kind": "pixel",
          "x": 10,
          "y": 45,
          "colour": "#ff0000",
          "describe": "the float is 50 tall and the block 40, so its last 10 rows are the float's"
        },
        {
          "kind": "pixel",
          "x": 60,
          "y": 45,
          "colour": "#ffffff",
          "describe": "and the block has ended by then, so nothing of it shows to the right of the float"
        },
        {
